meta {
  name: Upgrade Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/upgrade
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "app_version_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "values": { "replicas": 2, "image": { "tag": "v1.1.0" } },
    "secret_inputs": {}
  }
}

docs {
  Re-applies a deployment against a new (or the same) published AppVersion,
  optionally replacing values and/or secrets. Returns 202 Accepted;
  the orchestrator reconciles asynchronously — subscribe to /events for
  live progress.

  NOTE: the body:json block above uses the key "app_version_id" — this is
  incorrect. The handler expects "to_version_id". Update the key before sending.

  Request body:
    to_version_id      required UUID — must be a published version of the
                       same app as the existing deployment
    new_values         optional JSON object — if omitted, the existing
                       deployment values are reused unchanged
    new_secret_inputs  optional map<field, value> — new secrets to write
                       to the store; if omitted, existing secret refs are
                       forwarded unchanged

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; Deployer role; caller must own the deployment or be PlatformAdmin.
    2. Parse deployment ID — 404 if not found.
    3. Deployment must not be in a terminal or deleting state — 409 deployment_not_upgradeable.
    4. to_version_id must be a valid UUID, belong to the same app, and be published — 422 otherwise.
    5. new_values validated against the new version's values.schema.json; secret fields
       must appear in new_secret_inputs, not new_values — 422 on violation.
    6. New secrets written to the SecretStore at kv/data/deployments/<id>/<field>.
    7. Orchestrator.Apply called — on failure, state transitions to failed_orchestrator or
       pending_orchestrator (transient); on success, state set to applying.

  Responses:
    202 Accepted                   — updated deployment row (state=applying)
    401 unauthorized               — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden                  — caller does not own the deployment
    404 not_found                  — deployment or version not found
    409 deployment_not_upgradeable — deployment is in a terminal or deleting state
    422 validation_failed          — bad UUIDs, schema violation, or wrong app version
    502 orchestrator_apply_failed  — orchestrator rejected the spec
    503 orchestrator_not_configured — no ORCHESTRATOR_KIND set
    503 orchestrator_transient_error — orchestrator temporarily unavailable (retry queued)
    503 secrets_not_configured     — secret store absent and new_secret_inputs provided
}
